    author="Rachael Brennan via Google"
  />

  <FeatureGrid
    id="how-the-music-is-chosen-for-your-wedding"
    eyebrow="Your Music"
    heading="How the Music Is Chosen for Your Wedding"
    alt={true}
  >
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      <p>
        Every single person has their own personal soundtrack and tastes. During
        your consultation with DJ Misha, he'll get to know you and learn about
        what type of music will best represent your personality and the overall
        atmosphere you envision for your wedding.&nbsp;
      </p>
    </Fragment>

    <FeatureCard
      title="Getting to Know Your Style"
      icon="user"
      titleIsNotHeading={true}
    >
      <p>
        We'll have a conversation about your music preferences. We'll talk about
        songs, artists, genres, and epic concerts you've attended. With that
        knowledge DJ Misha will execute a one-of-a-kind DJ set and a performance
        that can only be heard on your wedding day.
      </p>
    </FeatureCard>

    <FeatureCard
      title="Choosing the Type of Music"
      icon="star"
      titleIsNotHeading={true}
    >
      <p>
        Generally, wedding playlists tend to be diverse, eclectic, and include
        many genres, styles, and songs that span a variety of energy levels.
        Professional wedding DJs understand this and strive to incorporate
        different styles of music to appeal to different generations of guests
        while keeping to the intended vision for the evening. That is exactly
        what makes a wedding DJ great and something DJ Misha excels at.&nbsp;
      </p>
      <p>
        Since every wedding is different, it is common to see couples create
        playlists with a variety of genres, like Top 40, R&amp;B, Hip Hop, 80s,
        90s, Rock, EDM, House Music, Top Dance Hits, and much more.
      </p>
      <p>
        Whatever your vision may be, DJ Misha wants to know, and he wants to
        make that vision a reality for you.&nbsp;
      </p>
    </FeatureCard>
    <FeatureCard
      title="Adding Live Saxophone into the Musical Mix"
      titleIsNotHeading={true}
      icon="lightbulb"
    >
      <p>
        To elevate your reception even further, DJ Misha frequently performs DJ
        sets with live saxophone player accompaniment. This combination of <a
          href="/dj-saxophone/">DJ and saxophone</a
